sections.s2_technical:
Before Java 5 — no covariant returns:

```java
// Parent:
public class AccountFactory {
    public Account create(String id) { return new Account(id); }
}

// Child (pre-Java 5): MUST return EXACT same type!
public class SavingsAccountFactory extends AccountFactory {
    @Override
    public Account create(String id) {  // returns Account, not SavingsAccount!
        return new SavingsAccount(id, new BigDecimal("0.04"));
    }
}

// Caller needs CAST:
SavingsAccountFactory factory = new SavingsAccountFactory();
Account account = factory.create("SAV001");                    // returns Account
SavingsAccount sa = (SavingsAccount) factory.create("SAV001"); // CAST needed!
// Ugly, error-prone, and the factory KNOWS it creates SavingsAccount — why hide it?
```

After Java 5 — covariant return:

```java
// Child (Java 5+): CAN return SUBTYPE!
public class SavingsAccountFactory extends AccountFactory {
    @Override
    public SavingsAccount create(String id) {  // returns SavingsAccount — COVARIANT!
        return new SavingsAccount(id, new BigDecimal("0.04"));
    }
}

// Caller through child reference — NO CAST:
SavingsAccountFactory factory = new SavingsAccountFactory();
SavingsAccount sa = factory.create("SAV001");  // returns SavingsAccount directly!
sa.getInterestRate();                           // no cast needed!

// Caller through parent reference — still works (returns Account):
AccountFactory baseFactory = new SavingsAccountFactory();
Account account = baseFactory.create("SAV001");  // returns Account (polymorphic)
// Actual object IS SavingsAccount, but variable type is Account.
```

Rules for covariant return types:

```java
// VALID covariant: return type is SUBTYPE of parent's return type
class Parent { Animal getAnimal() { return new Animal(); } }
class Child extends Parent {
    @Override Dog getAnimal() { return new Dog(); }  // Dog extends Animal ✅
}

// VALID: child narrows from Account to SavingsAccount
class AccountFactory { Account create() { ... } }
class SavingsFactory extends AccountFactory {
    @Override SavingsAccount create() { ... }  // SavingsAccount extends Account ✅
}

// INVALID: return type is SUPERTYPE (widening — NOT allowed!)
// class Child extends Parent {
//     @Override Animal getAnimal() { return new Animal(); }  // if parent returns Dog
// }
// ❌ Cannot widen return type — only narrow (subtype)!

// INVALID: completely unrelated type
// class Child extends Parent {
//     @Override String getAnimal() { ... }  // String is not a subtype of Animal!
// }
// ❌ COMPILE ERROR

// PRIMITIVES: covariant return does NOT apply to primitives!
// Parent returns int → child MUST return int (not long, not Integer)
```

Practical use cases in banking:

```java
// USE CASE 1: Factory pattern — cleaner API
public class LoanFactory {
    public Loan create(BigDecimal amount) { return new Loan(amount); }
}
public class HomeLoanFactory extends LoanFactory {
    @Override
    public HomeLoan create(BigDecimal amount) {  // returns HomeLoan!
        return new HomeLoan(amount, "RESIDENTIAL");
    }
}
HomeLoanFactory factory = new HomeLoanFactory();
HomeLoan hl = factory.create(new BigDecimal("5000000"));  // no cast!
hl.getPropertyType();  // HomeLoan-specific method — accessible!

// USE CASE 2: Builder pattern — fluent return
public class AccountBuilder {
    public AccountBuilder withName(String name) { this.name = name; return this; }
}
public class SavingsAccountBuilder extends AccountBuilder {
    @Override
    public SavingsAccountBuilder withName(String name) {  // covariant!
        super.withName(name);
        return this;
    }
    public SavingsAccountBuilder withRate(BigDecimal rate) { this.rate = rate; return this; }
}
// Fluent API: new SavingsAccountBuilder().withName("Rajesh").withRate(0.04)
// Without covariant: withName() returns AccountBuilder → can't chain withRate()!

// USE CASE 3: clone() — return actual type
public class Trade implements Cloneable {
    @Override
    public Trade clone() {  // returns Trade, not Object!
        return (Trade) super.clone();
    }
}
Trade original = new Trade("TRD-001");
Trade copy = original.clone();  // no cast! Object.clone() returns Object, but we return Trade.
```

