sections.s2_technical:
What a record generates automatically:

```java
// ONE LINE:
public record Trade(String tradeId, String symbol, BigDecimal amount) {}

// COMPILER GENERATES (equivalent to ~50 lines of POJO):
public final class Trade {
    private final String tradeId;       // private final — immutable!
    private final String symbol;
    private final BigDecimal amount;

    // Canonical constructor:
    public Trade(String tradeId, String symbol, BigDecimal amount) {
        this.tradeId = tradeId;
        this.symbol = symbol;
        this.amount = amount;
    }

    // Accessors (NOT getTradeId — just tradeId!):
    public String tradeId() { return tradeId; }
    public String symbol() { return symbol; }
    public BigDecimal amount() { return amount; }

    // equals: based on ALL components
    @Override public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (!(o instanceof Trade t)) return false;
        return Objects.equals(tradeId, t.tradeId)
            && Objects.equals(symbol, t.symbol)
            && Objects.equals(amount, t.amount);
    }

    // hashCode: based on ALL components
    @Override public int hashCode() { return Objects.hash(tradeId, symbol, amount); }

    // toString: shows all components
    @Override public String toString() {
        return "Trade[tradeId=" + tradeId + ", symbol=" + symbol + ", amount=" + amount + "]";
    }
}
// ALL of this from ONE LINE: record Trade(String tradeId, String symbol, BigDecimal amount) {}
```

Records support custom logic:

```java
public record Trade(String tradeId, String symbol, BigDecimal amount) {

    // COMPACT CONSTRUCTOR — validation without repeating assignments:
    public Trade {
        if (tradeId == null || tradeId.isBlank()) throw new IllegalArgumentException("tradeId required");
        if (amount.signum() < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("amount cannot be negative");
        // No this.tradeId = tradeId needed — compiler adds it!
    }

    // Custom methods:
    public boolean isLargeTrade() { return amount.compareTo(new BigDecimal("100000")) > 0; }

    // Static factory:
    public static Trade of(String id, String symbol, double amount) {
        return new Trade(id, symbol, BigDecimal.valueOf(amount));
    }

    // Records CAN implement interfaces:
    // public record Trade(...) implements Serializable, Comparable<Trade> { }
}
```

HOW records enforce OOP:

```java
// ENCAPSULATION: fields are private final — no setters, no mutation
Trade trade = new Trade("TRD-001", "RELIANCE", new BigDecimal("245050"));
// trade.tradeId = "HACKED";  → COMPILE ERROR! Field is private final.
// No setTradeId() method exists.

// VALUE SEMANTICS: two records with same data ARE equal
Trade t1 = new Trade("TRD-001", "RELIANCE", new BigDecimal("245050"));
Trade t2 = new Trade("TRD-001", "RELIANCE", new BigDecimal("245050"));
t1.equals(t2);  // TRUE — same component values
t1.hashCode() == t2.hashCode();  // TRUE — works in HashSet/HashMap!

// IMMUTABILITY: can safely share across threads
// No synchronization needed — record cannot be modified after construction.
```

When records are NOT suitable:

```java
// ❌ NOT for JPA entities:
// @Entity
// public record Account(String id, BigDecimal balance) {}
// PROBLEMS:
// 1. JPA requires no-arg constructor — records don't have one
// 2. JPA needs setters for dirty checking — records are immutable
// 3. JPA proxies need non-final class — records are final
// USE: regular class for JPA entities. Records for DTOs.

// ❌ NOT for mutable domain objects:
// You need account.setBalance(newBalance) — records don't support this.
// Records model DATA that doesn't change after creation.

// ❌ NOT for inheritance hierarchies:
// Records are implicitly final — cannot extend a record.
// class SpecialTrade extends Trade { }  → COMPILE ERROR!
// Records CAN implement interfaces, but CANNOT extend classes (except Object).

// ✅ PERFECT for:
// DTOs: record TradeResponse(String tradeId, BigDecimal amount, String status) {}
// Value objects: record Money(BigDecimal amount, String currency) {}
// Map keys: record CompositeKey(String accountId, LocalDate date) {}
// Event payloads: record TradeExecutedEvent(String tradeId, BigDecimal amount) {}
```

