LOW COHESION — the God class anti-pattern:

```java
// ❌ GOD CLASS: does EVERYTHING — 3000+ lines, 50+ methods, 20+ fields
public class BankingManager {
    // Account management:
    public Account createAccount(String name) { ... }
    public void closeAccount(String id) { ... }
    public BigDecimal getBalance(String id) { ... }

    // Trade execution:
    public Trade executeTrade(String symbol, int qty) { ... }
    public void cancelTrade(String tradeId) { ... }

    // Notification:
    public void sendSms(String phone, String msg) { ... }
    public void sendEmail(String email, String msg) { ... }

    // Reporting:
    public Report generateDailyReport() { ... }
    public Report generateMonthlyReport() { ... }

    // Fee calculation:
    public BigDecimal calculateBrokerage(BigDecimal amount) { ... }
    public BigDecimal calculateGST(BigDecimal brokerage) { ... }

    // Compliance:
    public boolean checkKYC(String customerId) { ... }
    public void submitRBIReport() { ... }

    // PROBLEMS:
    // 1. 3000 lines — impossible to understand quickly
    // 2. Changing fee logic might accidentally break notifications (same class!)
    // 3. Can't test fee calculation without loading account/trade/notification code
    // 4. Can't reuse FeeCalculation without dragging BankingManager
    // 5. Every developer touches this file → merge conflicts daily
}
```

HIGH COHESION — each class has ONE responsibility:

```java
// ✅ HIGH COHESION: each class does ONE thing well

public class AccountService {
    // ONLY account-related operations:
    public Account createAccount(String name) { ... }
    public void closeAccount(String id) { ... }
    public BigDecimal getBalance(String id) { ... }
}

public class TradeExecutionService {
    // ONLY trade-related operations:
    public Trade executeTrade(String symbol, int qty) { ... }
    public void cancelTrade(String tradeId) { ... }
}

public class NotificationService {
    // ONLY notification-related:
    public void sendSms(String phone, String msg) { ... }
    public void sendEmail(String email, String msg) { ... }
}

public class FeeCalculator {
    // ONLY fee-related:
    public BigDecimal calculateBrokerage(BigDecimal amount) { ... }
    public BigDecimal calculateGST(BigDecimal brokerage) { ... }
}

public class ComplianceService {
    // ONLY compliance-related:
    public boolean checkKYC(String customerId) { ... }
    public void submitRBIReport() { ... }
}

// BENEFITS:
// 1. Each class: 50-200 lines — easy to understand
// 2. Change fees → only FeeCalculator touched → notifications safe
// 3. Test FeeCalculator in isolation — no account/trade code loaded
// 4. Reuse FeeCalculator in ANY service — no baggage
// 5. Different developers work on different files → no merge conflicts
```

HOW to check if a class has high cohesion — the "AND" test:

```java
// Describe the class in ONE sentence. If you use "AND":
// "BankingManager creates accounts AND executes trades AND sends notifications AND calculates fees"
// → LOW cohesion! Multiple ANDs = multiple responsibilities.

// "FeeCalculator calculates trading fees"
// → HIGH cohesion! ONE sentence, NO "AND."

// "AccountService manages bank account lifecycle"
// → HIGH cohesion!
```

