`clone()` — shallow copy (covered in depth in Q14):

```java
public class Trade implements Cloneable {
    @Override
    public Trade clone() {
        try {
            return (Trade) super.clone();  // shallow copy — Object.clone() native method
        } catch (CloneNotSupportedException e) {
            throw new AssertionError();  // never happens — we implement Cloneable
        }
    }
}
// clone() is protected on Object — must override as public.
// Returns Object — must cast.
// Without Cloneable → CloneNotSupportedException.
// Shallow: primitives copied, object references SHARED.
// DISCOURAGED: prefer copy constructors or records.
```

`wait()` / `notify()` / `notifyAll()` — thread communication:

```java
// Producer-Consumer with shared queue:
public class TradeQueue {
    private final Queue<Trade> queue = new LinkedList<>();
    private static final int MAX = 10;

    // PRODUCER: adds trade, notifies waiting consumers
    public synchronized void produce(Trade trade) throws InterruptedException {
        while (queue.size() == MAX) {
            wait();  // queue full — RELEASE lock, SUSPEND this thread
            // ✅ Inside synchronized — has the monitor lock
        }
        queue.add(trade);
        notifyAll();  // wake up ALL waiting consumers
        // ✅ Inside synchronized — has the monitor lock
    }

    // CONSUMER: takes trade, notifies waiting producers
    public synchronized Trade consume() throws InterruptedException {
        while (queue.isEmpty()) {
            wait();  // queue empty — RELEASE lock, SUSPEND this thread
        }
        Trade trade = queue.poll();
        notifyAll();  // wake up ALL waiting producers
        return trade;
    }
}

// WHY synchronized is required:
// wait() releases the object's monitor lock — if you DON'T hold the lock, there's nothing to release!
// notify() wakes threads waiting on the object's monitor — if not synchronized, which monitor?
// Without synchronized: IllegalMonitorStateException at runtime!

// trade.wait();  // ❌ IllegalMonitorStateException! Not in synchronized block!
// synchronized(trade) { trade.wait(); }  // ✅ Holds trade's monitor lock.
```

`finalize()` — DEPRECATED:

```java
// OLD (deprecated since Java 9, removed in future):
@Override
protected void finalize() throws Throwable {
    // Called by GC before reclaiming memory. UNRELIABLE:
    // 1. No guarantee WHEN (or IF) it runs
    // 2. Slows down GC (objects put in finalization queue)
    // 3. Can resurrect objects (bad!)
    // 4. Exceptions silently swallowed
    closeConnection();  // ❌ DON'T rely on this!
}

// NEW: use Cleaner or try-with-resources:
public class DbConnection implements AutoCloseable {
    @Override
    public void close() {
        // Deterministic cleanup!
        connection.close();
    }
}
// try (var conn = new DbConnection()) { use(conn); } // close() called automatically!
